# Midwest Airbnb Listings: Data Dictionary

**Dataset:** `listings` table in `midwest_airbnb.db` (SQLite), 14,887 rows and 29 columns
**Source:** Inside Airbnb (https://insideairbnb.com/get-the-data/), the detailed `listings.csv.gz` file for each of three regions: Chicago (snapshot 2026-07-20), Columbus (snapshot 2026-07-23), and Twin Cities MSA (snapshot 2026-07-21). Column meanings follow Inside Airbnb's data dictionary and assumptions (https://insideairbnb.com/data-assumptions/).
**Course:** ISA 401, Miami University

> One row is one listing that showed a nightly price on the snapshot date; listings with no price were dropped. Empty cells are stored as SQL `NULL`.

---

## Field Definitions

| Field | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `city` | text | Which Inside Airbnb region the listing came from: `Chicago` (7,439 rows), `Columbus` (2,587), or `Twin Cities` (4,861). The Twin Cities file covers the Minneapolis-St. Paul metro area, not just the two cities. |
| `snapshot_date` | text | Date Inside Airbnb compiled the file, stored as an ISO text string, not a date: `2026-07-20` for Chicago, `2026-07-23` for Columbus, `2026-07-21` for Twin Cities. Every row of a city shares the same value. |
| `id` | text | Airbnb's listing id. Unique across the table (14,887 distinct values). Stored as text even though it looks numeric, so compare it to a quoted string. |
| `name` | text | Listing title as shown on Airbnb (for example "Tiny Studio Apartment 94 Walk Score"). Never empty. |
| `price` | real | Nightly price in U.S. dollars on the snapshot date, with the dollar sign and commas removed. Ranges from 2.56 to 11,412; never `NULL` (rows without a price were dropped). |
| `room_type` | text | Airbnb's four listing categories: `Entire home/apt` (11,652 rows), `Private room` (2,951), `Hotel room` (246), or `Shared room` (38). |
| `host_id` | text | Airbnb's unique id for the host account. 6,970 distinct hosts across 14,887 listings, so many hosts manage more than one property. Stored as text like `id`. |
| `host_name` | text | Host's first name as shown publicly (for example "Rebecca", "Sarah", "Elizabeth"). 3,328 distinct names. |
| `host_since` | text | Intended to be the date the host joined Airbnb. **Not populated in this extract** — all 14,887 rows are `NULL`. Do not filter or report on this column. |
| `host_is_superhost` | text | Whether Airbnb has granted the host Superhost status: `t` or `f`. A small number of rows are `NULL` where the host's status wasn't captured at snapshot time. |
| `neighbourhood` | text | Inside Airbnb's `neighbourhood_cleansed` field — a standardized neighborhood/area name within each city (for example "Hyde Park", "West Town", "Lincoln Park"). 119 distinct values across the three metro areas. |
| `latitude` | real | Listing's latitude, slightly jittered by Airbnb for host privacy. Ranges from 39.88 to 46.24 across the three metros. |
| `longitude` | real | Listing's longitude, slightly jittered by Airbnb for host privacy. Ranges from -94.53 to -82.78 across the three metros. |
| `property_type` | text | Airbnb's fine-grained property category, more specific than `room_type` (for example "Private room in condo", "Entire rental unit", "Room in boutique hotel"). 62 distinct values. |
| `accommodates` | integer | Maximum number of guests the listing sleeps. Ranges from 1 to 16. |
| `bedrooms` | real | Number of bedrooms. Ranges from 1 to 16; missing (`NULL`) for 2,976 listings (about 20%), often studio-style units where Airbnb doesn't require a bedroom count. |
| `beds` | real | Number of beds. Ranges from 1 to 32; missing for 668 listings. |
| `bathrooms_text` | text | Free-text bathroom count and type as written by the host (for example "1 bath", "1.5 baths", "1 shared bath"). 33 distinct values, so treat it as text, not a number, unless you parse it. |
| `minimum_nights` | integer | Fewest nights a guest can book in one reservation. Ranges from 1 to 365; missing for 15 listings. |
| `availability_365` | integer | Number of the next 365 days the listing's calendar shows as bookable, as of the snapshot date. Ranges from 0 (fully booked or blocked) to 365 (wide open). |
| `number_of_reviews` | integer | Total number of reviews the listing has ever received. Ranges from 0 to 2,246. |
| `number_of_reviews_ltm` | integer | Number of reviews received in the last twelve months ("ltm"). Ranges from 0 to 1,220. |
| `first_review` | text | Date of the listing's earliest review, as an ISO text string. Earliest value in the data is 2009-07-03; `NULL` for listings with no reviews yet. |
| `last_review` | text | Date of the listing's most recent review, as an ISO text string (for example "2026-06-08", "2026-06-30"). `NULL` for listings with no reviews yet. |
| `review_scores_rating` | real | Overall guest rating on Airbnb's 1–5 star scale. Ranges from 1 to 5; missing for 1,761 listings that have no reviews. |
| `reviews_per_month` | real | Average number of reviews per month since the listing's first review, a proxy for booking frequency. Ranges from 0.01 to 77.72; missing for the same 1,761 listings with no reviews. |
| `instant_bookable` | text | Intended to flag whether a guest can book without host approval: `t` or `f`. **Not populated in this extract** — all 14,887 rows are `NULL`. Do not filter or report on this column. |
| `estimated_revenue_l365d` | real | Inside Airbnb's modeled revenue estimate for the last 365 days (roughly price times estimated booked nights). Ranges from 0 to 1,114,800. Treat as an estimate, not billing data. |
| `amenities_count` | integer | Not an original Inside Airbnb column — computed for this course as the count of items in each listing's `amenities` list. Ranges from 0 to 100. |

---

## Notes

- `neighbourhood` is Inside Airbnb's `neighbourhood_cleansed` column, standardized by Inside Airbnb rather than the host's free-text neighborhood.
- `amenities_count` was derived for this course from the original `amenities` list column and is not part of Inside Airbnb's standard dictionary.
- `host_since` and `instant_bookable` are entirely missing in this extract; they're documented here for completeness but should not be used to filter, group, or chart.
